WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.402
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.760
Mr. Churchill will be
introduced by the American elder

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.535
statesman, Bernard Baruch.

00:00:17.535 --> 00:00:20.760
The program will be opened
by Dr. Karl T. Compton,

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.656
but before that, the national
anthem is being played.

00:00:24.656 --> 00:00:27.430
Dr. Compton is chairman
of the Corporation of MIT.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.923
[NATIONAL ANTHEM PLAYING]

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.050
Ladies and gentlemen,
Dr. Karl T. Compton.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:26.010
Mr. Churchill, Mr. Baruch,
distinguished guests, ladies

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.340
and gentlemen.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.570
May I first read the
following excerpt

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.880
from a letter received from the
White House, dated March 25th.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.120
My dear Dr. Compton,
I certainly regret

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.660
exceedingly that conditions
developed to the point

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.710
where I had to make a
cancellation at the last minute

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:49.770
for the Massachusetts Institute
of Technology appearance.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.410
I hope you will express
my sincere regret

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.570
to the members of the
faculty of the Massachusetts

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:58.520
Institute of Technology and
make it perfectly clear to them

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.880
that the cancellation
was not a voluntary one,

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.530
but was a case of necessity.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.190
I had a most pleasant evening
with the former prime minister

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.990
of Great Britain.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.510
Mr. Churchill, I am
sure, will give you

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.770
something that will be
historical for this period.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.501
Signed, Harry S. Truman.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:22.483
[APPLAUSE]

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:31.670
And now to introduce our
very distinguished guest

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.840
from overseas, I shall
call upon his old friend,

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.690
a very distinguished American.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.385
With deep feelings of
respect and affection,

00:02:41.385 --> 00:02:44.270
he is called chief
by all of those

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:48.080
who have had the rare
privilege of working under him.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.930
Those who have not had
this privilege also

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:55.460
admire him for his great
wisdom, high integrity,

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:59.330
and unswerving devotion to
the welfare of our country.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:03.280
The advisor to presidents,
America's elder statesman,

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.044
Mr. Bernard M. Baruch.

00:03:06.044 --> 00:03:09.032
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.980
Mr. Churchill,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.780
Last Sunday, from the
windows of my house,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.100
we watched a parade
celebrating the anniversary

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.770
of Greek independence.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:44.740
Men, women, and
toddling children

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:50.790
marched through cheering crowds,
composed of all races, creeds,

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.190
and colors.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:04:00.030
The man who honors us tonight
turned suddenly to me and said

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:06.420
with deep emotion, you see,
you cannot quench freedom.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.680
That thought is
the driving force

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:16.769
of this peace-hungering
man who feels so deeply

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:23.580
for those who suffer the blood,
sweat, and tears of life.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.210
With a deep sympathy
for the unfortunate,

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.918
he has a daring
contempt for the bully.

00:04:31.918 --> 00:04:34.950
Through the 30
years I have known

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:40.740
him, in his darkest
moments, although always

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:44.460
mindful of his
country's welfare,

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.710
I have never known him to
make an ignoble proposal.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:55.230
I present the greatest
living Englishman,

00:04:55.230 --> 00:05:01.440
the finest flowering of
leadership and statesmanship

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.820
that England ever produced,
the right honorable Winston

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:06.727
Churchill.

00:05:06.727 --> 00:05:10.206
[APPLAUSE]

00:05:51.457 --> 00:06:04.920
Dr. Compton, your excellency,
ladies and gentlemen,

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:11.350
I am honored by your wish
that I should take part

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:15.220
in the discussions
of the Massachusetts

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.940
Institute of Technology.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.980
We have suffered
in Great Britain

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:25.420
by the lack of colleges
of university rank

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:30.340
in which engineering and the
allied subjects are taught.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:35.370
Industrial production
depends on technology,

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:41.020
and it is because the Americans,
like the pre-war Germans,

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:47.860
have realized this and created
institutions for the advanced

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:53.510
training of large numbers
of high-grade engineers

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:59.050
to translate the advantages of
pure science into industrial

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:00.790
technique--

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.000
it is for that reason
that their output

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:10.540
per head and constant
standard of life are so high.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:16.780
It is surprising that England,
which was the first country

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:23.410
to be industrialized, has
nothing of comparable stature.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:27.055
If tonight, I strike
other notes than those

00:07:27.055 --> 00:07:32.110
of material progress,
it implies no

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:37.000
want of admiration for
all the work you have done

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.920
and are doing.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:42.400
My aim, like yours,
is to be guided

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.937
by balance and proportions.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:52.810
The outstanding feature
of the 20th century

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:58.210
has been the enormous
expansion in the numbers who

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.420
are given the
opportunity to share

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:07.420
in the larger and more varied
life, which in previous periods

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:13.060
was reserved for the few
and for the very few.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:19.510
This process must continue
at an increasing rate.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.790
If we are bring
the broad message

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:29.740
of the people in every land
to the table of abundance,

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:37.600
it can only be by the tireless
improvement of all our means

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:42.730
of technical production
and by the diffusion

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:47.780
in every form of education
of an improved quality

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:52.690
to scores of millions
of men and women.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:57.430
Even in this darkening
hour, I have faith

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:01.150
that this process will go on.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:07.840
I rejoice in Tennyson's
celebrated lines--

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:12.280
men, my brothers,
men, the workers,

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:16.480
ever reaping something
new, that which

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:21.440
they have done but earnest of
the things that they shall do.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:28.740
I was, however, a
little disquieted,

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:33.870
I must admit, that you
found it necessary to debate

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:38.880
the question, to quote Dr.
[? Bertrad's ?] opening

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:48.480
address, of whether the
problem of world production,

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:53.730
yielding at least a minimum
living to the whole population,

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.540
can be solved and whether
man has so destroyed

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.120
the resources of his
world that they may

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.330
be doomed to die of starvation.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:08.910
If, with all resources
of modern science,

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:13.610
we find ourselves unable
to avert world famine,

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.770
we shall all be to blame.

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:21.510
But a peculiar responsibility
would rest upon the scientists.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:27.210
I do not believe that they
will fail, but if they do--

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.490
or perhaps were not
allowed to succeed--

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:34.710
the consequences would
be very unpleasant,

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:39.390
because it is quite certain
that mankind would not

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:42.750
agree to starve equally.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:45.060
And there might be some
very sharp disagreements

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:48.894
about how the last
crust was to be shared.

00:10:48.894 --> 00:10:53.670
[LAUGHTER]

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:57.550
As our greatest
intellectual authorities

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:03.700
here will readily admit, that
would simplify our problem

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.254
in an unduly primordial manner.

00:11:06.254 --> 00:11:09.890
[LAUGHTER]

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.760
Ladies and gentlemen,
I frankly confess

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:17.200
that I feel somewhat
overawed in addressing

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:24.180
this vast scientific and learned
audience on the subjects which

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:28.280
your panels are discussing.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:33.860
I have no technical and
no university education.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.253
I have just had to pick up a
few things as I went along.

00:11:37.253 --> 00:11:40.634
[LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE]

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.442
Therefore, I speak
with a diffidence,

00:11:53.442 --> 00:11:57.554
which I hope to
overcome as I proceed,

00:11:57.554 --> 00:12:04.770
on these profound scientific,
social, and philosophic issues,

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:10.180
each of which [INAUDIBLE] a
life-long study for itself

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:15.640
and are now to be examined,
as school men would say,

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:20.500
not only in their integrity,
but in their relationships,

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:24.010
meaning thereby not only
one-by-one, but all together.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:31.520
I was so glad that in
the first instance,

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.960
you asked me to
talk about the past,

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:38.320
rather than to peer
into the future,

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.360
because I know
more about the past

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:44.010
than I do about the future.

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:48.870
And I was well content that the
President of the United States,

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:52.480
whose gift of prophesy
was so remarkably

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:56.286
vindicated by recent
electoral results--

00:12:56.286 --> 00:12:58.676
[APPLAUSE]

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:07.110
--though shouldn't have
accepted that cost.

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:11.790
We all regret that his heavy
state duties prevent him

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:14.820
from being there tonight.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:19.185
I shall therefore have to try
to do a little of the peering

00:13:19.185 --> 00:13:19.685
myself.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:29.770
Ladies and gentleman,
for us in Britain,

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:35.830
the 19th century ended amid the
glories of the Victorian era,

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:40.360
and we entered upon the dawn
of the 20th in high hope

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:45.340
for our country, our
empire, and the world.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:45.840
The

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:49.670
Latter and larger part
of the 19th century

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:52.930
had been the period
of liberal advance--

00:13:52.930 --> 00:14:04.100
liberal with a small
L. In 1900, a sense

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:09.810
of moving hopefully forward to
brighter, broader, and easier

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:12.320
days was predominant.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:16.220
Little did we guess that
what is being called

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:20.130
the century of the
common man would witness

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:25.520
as its outstanding feature
more common men killing

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:29.770
each other with greater
facilities than any other five

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:33.080
centuries put together in
the history of the world.

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:41.450
But we entered this terrible
20th century with confidence.

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:45.350
We thought that with
improving transportation,

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:49.010
nations would get to
know each other better.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:53.330
We believed that as they got
to know each other better,

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:58.130
they would like each other more,
and that national rivalries

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:04.550
would fade in a growing
international consciousness.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:10.100
We took it almost for granted
that science would confer

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:13.366
continued [? boons ?]
and blessings upon us,

00:15:13.366 --> 00:15:17.730
would give us better meals,
better garments, and better

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:22.940
dwellings for less trouble,
and thus steadily shorten

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:27.900
the hours of labor and leave
more time for play and culture.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:35.380
In the name of ordered
but unceasing progress,

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:41.020
we saluted the age of democracy,
democracy expressing itself

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:45.250
ever more widely
through parliaments

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:52.560
freely and fairly elected on a
broad or universal franchise.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:56.610
We saw no reason then why
men and women should not

00:15:56.610 --> 00:16:03.232
shape their own home life and
careers without being cramped

00:16:03.232 --> 00:16:06.660
by the growing complexity
of the state, which

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:12.840
was to be their servant and
the protector or their rights.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:16.060
You had the famous
American maxim--

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:18.810
governments derive
their just powers

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:21.450
from the consent
of the governed.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:24.840
And we both noticed
that the world

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:29.280
was divided into peoples
that owned the governments

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:32.370
and governments that
owned the peoples.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:36.170
At least I heard all
this around that time,

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:40.300
and I liked some
of it very much.

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:45.670
[INAUDIBLE] minister in the
British Liberal government--

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:49.620
with a large L,
please, this time--

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:55.720
returned by a great
majority in 1906.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:17:00.000
That new liberal
government arrived in power

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.260
with much of its message already
delivered and most of it's aims

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:07.476
already achieved.

00:17:07.476 --> 00:17:11.099
The days of hereditary
aristocratic privilege

00:17:11.099 --> 00:17:13.266
were ended or numbered.

00:17:13.266 --> 00:17:18.660
The path was open for talent
in every field of endeavor.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:22.440
Primary education was
compulsory, universal,

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.424
and free--

00:17:23.424 --> 00:17:26.339
or about to become so.

00:17:26.339 --> 00:17:29.740
New problems,
arising as problems

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:36.450
due from former successes,
awaited the new administration.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:40.560
The independence of
the [? proletarium, ?]

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.020
the independence of
the proletariat from

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:48.240
[? thralldom ?] involved
at least a minimum standard

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:53.730
of life and labor and security
for old age, sickness,

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:57.750
and the death of the
family breadwinner.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:04.140
It was to these costs of social
reform and social insurance

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:07.770
that we addressed ourselves.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:10.320
Ladies and gentlemen,
the name of Lloyd George

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.510
will never be associated
in Great Britain

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:14.540
with its new departure.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:18.770
I am proud to have been its
lieutenant in this work,

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:23.800
and also later as a conservative
chancellor of the [INAUDIBLE],,

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:28.441
and later still as head of the
wartime national coalition,

00:18:28.441 --> 00:18:32.850
to have carried these
same themes forward

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:34.350
on a magnified scale.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:39.680
That's how we began the century.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:46.710
Science presently placed
novel and dangerous facilities

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:50.176
in the hands of the
most powerful countries.

00:18:50.176 --> 00:18:53.190
[INAUDIBLE] humanity
was informed

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.930
that it could make
machines that would

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:59.900
fly through the air
and vessels which

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:04.380
could swim beneath the
surface of the seas.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:10.440
The conquest of the air and the
perfection of the art of flying

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:14.730
fulfilled the dream which
for thousands of years

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:18.660
had glittered in
human imagination.

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:23.620
Certainly, it was a
marvelous and romantic event.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:27.078
Whether the bestowal
of this gift

00:19:27.078 --> 00:19:33.734
upon an immature civilization,
composed of competing nations

00:19:33.734 --> 00:19:40.140
whose nationalism grew with
every advance of democracy,

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:45.560
and who was yet devoid of
international organization--

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:50.466
whether this gift was
a blessing or a curse

00:19:50.466 --> 00:19:53.100
has yet to be proved.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:57.360
On the whole, I
remain an optimist.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:03.210
For good or for ill, air mastery
is today the supreme expression

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:05.296
of military power.

00:20:05.296 --> 00:20:11.130
And fleets and armies,
however vital and important,

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.760
must accept a subordinate rank.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:21.840
This is a memorable milestone
in the march of man.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:25.820
The submarine could
do it justice.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:29.400
I've never made any claim
to be a blessing or even

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:32.750
a convenience.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:40.100
I well remember when it
became an accomplished fact

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.460
of peculiar military
significance

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:46.850
to the British Isles
and to the British Navy.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:51.490
There was a general belief,
even in the admiral [INAUDIBLE],,

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:54.880
where I presided, that
no nation would ever

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:59.040
be so wicked as to use these
underwater vessels to sink

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:01.550
merchantmen at sea.

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:04.390
How could a submarine,
it was asked,

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:08.240
provide for the safety of
the crews, of the merchant

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:10.176
ships it sank?

00:21:10.176 --> 00:21:14.290
And public opinion was shocked
when old Admiral Fisher bluntly

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:19.250
declared that this would be
no bar to the submarine's

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:24.070
being used by the new and
growing German Navy in the most

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:26.850
ruthless manner.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:30.880
His prediction was
certainly not stultified

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:34.355
by what was soon to happen.

00:21:34.355 --> 00:21:38.020
Here then we have
these two novel

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:41.430
and potent weapons
placed in the hands

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:44.860
of highly nationalized,
sovereign states

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:48.890
in the early part
of the 20th century.

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:51.790
And both of them
dwell with us today

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:56.992
for our future edification.

00:21:56.992 --> 00:22:00.190
A third unmeasured
sphere opened to us

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:03.520
as the years passed,
which for the sake

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:08.690
of comprehensive brevity
I will describe as radar.

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:13.980
This radar, with its innumerable
variance in possibilities,

00:22:13.980 --> 00:22:18.290
had so far been the
handmaiden of the air.

00:22:18.290 --> 00:22:22.180
But it has also been the
enemy of the submarine,

00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:26.600
and in alliance with the air
may well prove its exterminator.

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:39.510
Thus, we see the changes which
were brought upon our society.

00:22:39.510 --> 00:22:42.970
In the first half
of the 20th century,

00:22:42.970 --> 00:22:49.050
and by the crimson wings of
war, the conquest of the air

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:53.240
affected profoundly
human affairs.

00:22:53.240 --> 00:22:56.950
It made the globe seem
much bigger to the mind

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:00.010
and much smaller to the body.

00:23:00.010 --> 00:23:06.070
The human biped was able to
travel about far more quickly.

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:09.670
This greatly reduced
the size of his estate,

00:23:09.670 --> 00:23:13.874
while at the same time
creating an even keener sense

00:23:13.874 --> 00:23:17.170
of its exploitable value.

00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:22.660
In the 19th century, Jules
Verne wrote Around the World

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:24.850
in 80 Days.

00:23:24.850 --> 00:23:27.400
It seemed a prodigy.

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.650
Now you can get
round it in four,

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:33.166
but you do not see
much of it on your way.

00:23:33.166 --> 00:23:35.650
[LAUGHTER]

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:38.660
The whole prospect
and outlook of mankind

00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:44.530
grew really immeasurably larger,
and the multiplication of ideas

00:23:44.530 --> 00:23:48.540
also proceeded at
an incredible rate.

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:53.420
This vast expansion
was unhappily not

00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:59.590
accompanied by any noticeable
advance in the stature of man,

00:23:59.590 --> 00:24:03.910
either in his mental faculties
or his moral character.

00:24:03.910 --> 00:24:08.560
His brain got no better,
but it bounced the more.

00:24:08.560 --> 00:24:11.060
[? Though ?] the scale
of events around him

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:14.240
assumed gigantic
proportions while he

00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:17.810
remained about the same size.

00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:23.150
By comparison, therefore, he
actually became much smaller.

00:24:23.150 --> 00:24:29.150
We no longer had great men
directing manageable affairs.

00:24:29.150 --> 00:24:34.340
Our need was the discipline and
array of gigantic and turbulent

00:24:34.340 --> 00:24:39.790
[? fact. ?] To this
task, we have certainly

00:24:39.790 --> 00:24:42.700
so far proved unequal.

00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:49.010
Science bestowed immense new
powers, and at the same time

00:24:49.010 --> 00:24:51.680
created conditions
which were largely

00:24:51.680 --> 00:24:58.050
beyond its comprehension, and
still more beyond its control.

00:24:58.050 --> 00:25:02.125
While he nursed the
illusion of growing mastery

00:25:02.125 --> 00:25:05.420
and exulted his
new trappings, he

00:25:05.420 --> 00:25:10.060
became the sport, and
presently the victim,

00:25:10.060 --> 00:25:16.050
of tides and currents, or
whirlpools and tornadoes,

00:25:16.050 --> 00:25:19.025
amid which he was far
more helpless than he

00:25:19.025 --> 00:25:20.270
had been for a long time.

00:25:23.780 --> 00:25:28.190
Hopeful developments
in many directions

00:25:28.190 --> 00:25:33.580
were proceeding in 1914 on
both sides of the Atlantic,

00:25:33.580 --> 00:25:38.090
and they seemed to point to
an age of peace and plenty,

00:25:38.090 --> 00:25:42.490
when suddenly violent
events broke in upon them.

00:25:42.490 --> 00:25:44.210
For more than 20
years, there had

00:25:44.210 --> 00:25:48.060
been no major war in Europe.

00:25:48.060 --> 00:25:52.512
Indeed, since the Civil
War in the United States,

00:25:52.512 --> 00:25:55.000
there had been no great
struggle in the West.

00:25:58.656 --> 00:26:02.640
A spirit of adventure
stirred the minds of men

00:26:02.640 --> 00:26:06.110
and was by no means allayed
by the general advance

00:26:06.110 --> 00:26:09.230
of prosperity and science.

00:26:09.230 --> 00:26:13.260
On the contrary,
prosperity meant power,

00:26:13.260 --> 00:26:16.220
and science offered weapons.

00:26:16.220 --> 00:26:18.170
We read in the Bible--

00:26:18.170 --> 00:26:21.620
I hope you still
read the Bible--

00:26:21.620 --> 00:26:24.996
Jeshurun waxed fat and kicked.

00:26:24.996 --> 00:26:27.850
For several
generations, Britannia

00:26:27.850 --> 00:26:32.600
had ruled the waves for
long periods at less cost

00:26:32.600 --> 00:26:37.090
annually than that of a
single modern battleship.

00:26:37.090 --> 00:26:41.830
History, I think,
ladies and gentlemen--

00:26:41.830 --> 00:26:46.180
history will say that this
great trust was not abused.

00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:49.730
American testimony about the
early period of the Monroe

00:26:49.730 --> 00:26:52.040
Doctrine is upon records.

00:26:52.040 --> 00:26:56.510
That was the suppression of the
slave trade [? embarrassing. ?]

00:26:56.510 --> 00:26:59.660
During our prolonged
Naval supremacy,

00:26:59.660 --> 00:27:03.590
undeterred by the rise
of foreign [INAUDIBLE],,

00:27:03.590 --> 00:27:08.640
we kept our ports freely open
to the commerce of the world.

00:27:08.640 --> 00:27:13.850
Our colonial and oriental
empire, even our coastal trade,

00:27:13.850 --> 00:27:18.210
was free to the shipping of
all the nations on equal terms.

00:27:18.210 --> 00:27:22.970
We in no way sought to obstruct
the right of other states

00:27:22.970 --> 00:27:24.630
or navies.

00:27:24.630 --> 00:27:27.380
For nearly the whole
of the 19th century,

00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:30.635
the monopoly of sea
power in British hands

00:27:30.635 --> 00:27:34.000
was a trust
discharged faithfully

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:35.150
in the general interest.

00:27:38.055 --> 00:27:40.953
[APPLAUSE]

00:27:45.310 --> 00:27:50.370
But in the first decade
of the 20th century,

00:27:50.370 --> 00:27:54.290
with new patterns of
warships, naval rivalries

00:27:54.290 --> 00:27:56.820
became acute and fierce.

00:27:56.820 --> 00:28:01.940
Civilized governments began
to think in dreadnoughts.

00:28:01.940 --> 00:28:05.590
It was in such a setting
[INAUDIBLE] to prevent

00:28:05.590 --> 00:28:08.130
the First World War--

00:28:08.130 --> 00:28:10.170
far more difficult
than it would have been

00:28:10.170 --> 00:28:13.434
to have prevented the second.

00:28:13.434 --> 00:28:19.080
There was, of course,
one way to prevent it,

00:28:19.080 --> 00:28:22.260
one way then as now--

00:28:22.260 --> 00:28:26.130
the creation of an international
instrument strong enough

00:28:26.130 --> 00:28:30.690
to adjust the
disputes of nations

00:28:30.690 --> 00:28:35.620
and enforce its decisions
against an aggressor.

00:28:35.620 --> 00:28:39.810
Much wisdom, eloquence,
and earnest effort

00:28:39.810 --> 00:28:43.710
was devoted to this theme in
which the United States took

00:28:43.710 --> 00:28:48.910
the lead, but we only got as far
as the World Court at the Hague

00:28:48.910 --> 00:28:53.080
and improvements in
the Geneva Convention.

00:28:53.080 --> 00:28:56.850
The impulses towards a
trial of strength in Europe

00:28:56.850 --> 00:29:00.720
were far stronger at this time.

00:29:00.720 --> 00:29:04.880
Germany demanding
her place in the sun

00:29:04.880 --> 00:29:08.550
was faced by a resolute
France with a military honor

00:29:08.550 --> 00:29:10.950
to regain.

00:29:10.950 --> 00:29:15.810
England, in accordance with our
foreign policy of 300 years,

00:29:15.810 --> 00:29:18.930
sustained the weak outside.

00:29:18.930 --> 00:29:23.120
France found an ally in
the Russia of the czars,

00:29:23.120 --> 00:29:27.610
and Germany in the crumbling
empire of the Habsburgs.

00:29:27.610 --> 00:29:31.180
The United States,
for reasons which

00:29:31.180 --> 00:29:35.030
were natural and
traditional, but no longer so

00:29:35.030 --> 00:29:40.020
[? varied ?] as in
the past, stood aloof

00:29:40.020 --> 00:29:44.400
and expected to be able
to watch as a spectator

00:29:44.400 --> 00:29:48.870
the thrilling, fearful drama
unfold from across what was

00:29:48.870 --> 00:29:52.605
then called the broad Atlantic.

00:29:52.605 --> 00:29:57.330
Though these expectations,
as you perhaps may remember,

00:29:57.330 --> 00:29:59.480
were not wholly borne
out by what happened.

00:30:02.610 --> 00:30:09.510
After four years of hideous
mechanical slaughter,

00:30:09.510 --> 00:30:14.520
illuminated by
infinite sacrifice,

00:30:14.520 --> 00:30:19.380
but not remarkably relieved
by strategy or generalship,

00:30:19.380 --> 00:30:24.660
the victorious Allies
assembled at Versailles.

00:30:24.660 --> 00:30:29.870
High hopes and spacious
opportunities awaited them.

00:30:29.870 --> 00:30:32.730
War stripped of
every pretension,

00:30:32.730 --> 00:30:36.000
of glamor or romance,
had been brought home

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:40.140
to the masses of the peoples,
and brought home in forms

00:30:40.140 --> 00:30:44.565
never before experienced,
except by the defeated.

00:30:44.565 --> 00:30:49.440
To stop another war was
the supreme object and duty

00:30:49.440 --> 00:30:54.210
of the statesmen who met
as friends and allies

00:30:54.210 --> 00:30:56.870
around the peace table.

00:30:56.870 --> 00:30:59.760
They made great errors.

00:30:59.760 --> 00:31:02.250
The doctrine of
self-determination

00:31:02.250 --> 00:31:05.110
was not the remedy
for Europe, which

00:31:05.110 --> 00:31:12.410
needed then, above all things,
unity and larger groupings.

00:31:12.410 --> 00:31:14.250
The idea that the
vanquished could

00:31:14.250 --> 00:31:18.520
pay the expenses of the victors
was a destructive and crazy

00:31:18.520 --> 00:31:20.820
delusion.

00:31:20.820 --> 00:31:25.140
The failure to strangle
Bolshevism at its birth

00:31:25.140 --> 00:31:28.020
and to bring Russia,
then prostrate,

00:31:28.020 --> 00:31:32.300
by one means or another into
the general democratic system

00:31:32.300 --> 00:31:36.390
lies heavy upon us today.

00:31:36.390 --> 00:31:40.500
Nevertheless, the
statesmen at Versailles,

00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:44.730
largely at the inspiration
of President Wilson,

00:31:44.730 --> 00:31:49.720
an inspiration implemented
effectively by British thought,

00:31:49.720 --> 00:31:51.860
created the League of Nations.

00:31:51.860 --> 00:31:55.165
This is our defense
before history,

00:31:55.165 --> 00:32:01.380
and had the league been
resolutely sustained and used,

00:32:01.380 --> 00:32:05.640
it would have saved us all.

00:32:05.640 --> 00:32:07.590
This was not to be.

00:32:07.590 --> 00:32:12.330
Another ordeal even more
appalling than the first

00:32:12.330 --> 00:32:14.670
lay before us.

00:32:14.670 --> 00:32:18.990
Even when so much
else had failed,

00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:23.320
we could have obtained
a prolonged peace,

00:32:23.320 --> 00:32:26.400
lasting all our lives
at least, simply

00:32:26.400 --> 00:32:30.570
by keeping Germany disarmed
in accordance with the treaty,

00:32:30.570 --> 00:32:34.060
and by treating her with
justice and magnanimity.

00:32:34.060 --> 00:32:36.350
This latter condition
was very nearly

00:32:36.350 --> 00:32:42.850
achieved at [INAUDIBLE] in 1925.

00:32:42.850 --> 00:32:45.420
But the failure to
enforce the disarmament

00:32:45.420 --> 00:32:50.130
clauses, and above all to
sustain the League of Nations--

00:32:50.130 --> 00:32:54.120
both of which purposes could
easily have been accomplished--

00:32:54.120 --> 00:32:56.190
brought upon us the
Second World War.

00:32:59.420 --> 00:33:03.950
Once again, the English-speaking
world gloriously but narrowly

00:33:03.950 --> 00:33:08.680
emerged, bleeding
and breathless,

00:33:08.680 --> 00:33:13.628
but united as we
never were before.

00:33:13.628 --> 00:33:16.068
[APPLAUSE]

00:33:22.412 --> 00:33:27.200
This unity is our
present salvation,

00:33:27.200 --> 00:33:29.210
because after all
our victories, we

00:33:29.210 --> 00:33:34.320
are now faced by perils
both grave and near,

00:33:34.320 --> 00:33:37.580
and by problems more
dire than have ever

00:33:37.580 --> 00:33:41.330
confronted Christian
civilization, even

00:33:41.330 --> 00:33:45.525
in this 20th century
of storm and change.

00:33:48.430 --> 00:33:53.080
There remains, however,
a key of deliverance.

00:33:53.080 --> 00:33:58.550
It is the same key which
was searched for by those

00:33:58.550 --> 00:34:02.960
who labored to set up the
World Court at the Hague

00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:05.790
in the early years
of the century.

00:34:05.790 --> 00:34:09.650
It is the same
conception which animated

00:34:09.650 --> 00:34:13.880
President Wilson and his
colleagues at Versailles--

00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:18.199
namely, the creation
of a world instrument

00:34:18.199 --> 00:34:22.400
capable, at least, of
giving to all its members

00:34:22.400 --> 00:34:25.931
security against aggression.

00:34:25.931 --> 00:34:28.940
The United Nations
organization, which

00:34:28.940 --> 00:34:32.480
has been created
under the inspiring

00:34:32.480 --> 00:34:35.750
leadership of my great
wartime friend, President

00:34:35.750 --> 00:34:39.730
Roosevelt, that organization--

00:34:39.730 --> 00:34:48.230
[APPLAUSE]

00:34:48.230 --> 00:34:51.929
--which took the place
of the former league,

00:34:51.929 --> 00:34:55.630
has so far been
rent and distracted

00:34:55.630 --> 00:34:59.060
by the antagonism
of Soviet Russia

00:34:59.060 --> 00:35:02.004
and by the fundamental
schism which

00:35:02.004 --> 00:35:07.230
was opened between communism
and the rest of mankind.

00:35:07.230 --> 00:35:09.250
But we must not despair.

00:35:09.250 --> 00:35:11.951
We must persevere.

00:35:11.951 --> 00:35:15.470
And if the gulf
continues to widen,

00:35:15.470 --> 00:35:19.730
we must make sure that
the cause of freedom

00:35:19.730 --> 00:35:25.100
is defended by all the resources
of combined forethought

00:35:25.100 --> 00:35:27.670
and superior science.

00:35:27.670 --> 00:35:35.150
Here lies the best hope of
averting a third world struggle

00:35:35.150 --> 00:35:40.340
and a sure means of coming
through it without being

00:35:40.340 --> 00:35:42.200
enslaved or destroyed.

00:35:42.200 --> 00:35:44.640
[APPLAUSE]

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:04.960
One of the questions which
you are debating here

00:36:04.960 --> 00:36:09.500
is defined as the failure
of social and political

00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:16.050
institutions to keep pace with
material and technical trends.

00:36:16.050 --> 00:36:18.850
Scientists should never
underrate the deep-seated

00:36:18.850 --> 00:36:21.760
qualities of human
nature, and how,

00:36:21.760 --> 00:36:26.140
repressed in one direction,
they will certainly

00:36:26.140 --> 00:36:28.086
break out in another.

00:36:28.086 --> 00:36:32.890
The genus Homo-- if I
may display my Latin.

00:36:32.890 --> 00:36:36.640
I have some, not much.

00:36:36.640 --> 00:36:39.975
The genus Homo is
a tough creature

00:36:39.975 --> 00:36:43.870
who has traveled here
by a very long road.

00:36:43.870 --> 00:36:48.040
His nature has been
shaped and his virtues

00:36:48.040 --> 00:36:54.530
ingrained by many millions
of years of struggle, fear,

00:36:54.530 --> 00:36:56.360
and pain.

00:36:56.360 --> 00:37:00.073
And its spirit has, from the
earliest dawn of history,

00:37:00.073 --> 00:37:05.060
shown itself upon occasion
capable of mounting

00:37:05.060 --> 00:37:09.680
to the sublime far above
material conditions

00:37:09.680 --> 00:37:12.420
or mortal terrors.

00:37:12.420 --> 00:37:16.690
He still remains--
man still remains--

00:37:16.690 --> 00:37:22.310
as Pope described
him 200 years ago.

00:37:22.310 --> 00:37:27.410
Placed on the isthmus
of this middle state,

00:37:27.410 --> 00:37:31.750
a being darkly wise
and rudely great,

00:37:31.750 --> 00:37:36.050
created half the rise
and half the fall,

00:37:36.050 --> 00:37:39.890
great lord of all things,
yet a prey to all.

00:37:39.890 --> 00:37:43.700
Sole judge of truth
in endless error

00:37:43.700 --> 00:37:48.050
hurled the glory, jest,
and riddle of the world.

00:37:53.250 --> 00:38:01.770
In his introductory
address, Dr. [? Bertrad, ?]

00:38:01.770 --> 00:38:06.030
the dean of humanities,
spoke with awe

00:38:06.030 --> 00:38:12.750
of an approaching scientific
ability to control

00:38:12.750 --> 00:38:16.320
men's thoughts with precision.

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:19.650
I should be very
content personally

00:38:19.650 --> 00:38:23.000
if my task in this world is
done before that happens.

00:38:26.130 --> 00:38:26.630
[INAUDIBLE]

00:38:26.630 --> 00:38:29.510
[APPLAUSE]

00:38:32.870 --> 00:38:37.610
Laws just or unjust may
govern men's actions.

00:38:37.610 --> 00:38:41.870
Tyrannies may restrain
or regulate their words.

00:38:41.870 --> 00:38:45.340
The machinery of propaganda
may pack their minds

00:38:45.340 --> 00:38:48.380
with falsehoods
and deny them truth

00:38:48.380 --> 00:38:51.330
for many generations of time.

00:38:51.330 --> 00:38:56.950
But the soul of man,
thus held in a trance

00:38:56.950 --> 00:39:00.080
nor frozen in a
long night, can be

00:39:00.080 --> 00:39:06.230
awakened by a spark coming
from God knows where.

00:39:06.230 --> 00:39:08.270
And in a moment,
the whole structure

00:39:08.270 --> 00:39:13.310
of lies and oppression
is on trial for its life.

00:39:13.310 --> 00:39:17.450
Peoples in bondage
need never despair.

00:39:17.450 --> 00:39:24.110
Let them hope and trust
in the genius of mankind.

00:39:24.110 --> 00:39:27.280
Science no doubt, if
sufficiently perverted,

00:39:27.280 --> 00:39:29.800
could exterminate us all.

00:39:29.800 --> 00:39:34.826
But it is not in the power at
present of material forces--

00:39:34.826 --> 00:39:38.830
at present or in any period
which the youngest here tonight

00:39:38.830 --> 00:39:41.790
need take into
practical account,

00:39:41.790 --> 00:39:46.670
to alter permanently the
main elements in human nature

00:39:46.670 --> 00:39:50.620
and restrict the
infinite variety of forms

00:39:50.620 --> 00:39:54.200
in which the soul and
genius of the human race

00:39:54.200 --> 00:39:57.980
can and will express itself.

00:39:57.980 --> 00:40:04.460
How right you are, Dr. Compton,
in this great institution

00:40:04.460 --> 00:40:06.750
of technical study
and achievement,

00:40:06.750 --> 00:40:12.590
to keep a dean of
humanities and to give him

00:40:12.590 --> 00:40:16.770
so commanding a part to
play in your discussion.

00:40:16.770 --> 00:40:19.734
[APPLAUSE]

00:40:23.200 --> 00:40:26.440
No technical knowledge
can outweigh knowledge

00:40:26.440 --> 00:40:31.090
of the humanities, in the
gaining of which philosophy

00:40:31.090 --> 00:40:34.570
and history walk hand-in-hand.

00:40:34.570 --> 00:40:37.600
Our inheritance of
well-founded, slowly

00:40:37.600 --> 00:40:41.730
conceived codes
of honor, morals,

00:40:41.730 --> 00:40:46.000
and manners, the
passionate convictions,

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:49.550
which so many hundreds of
millions share together,

00:40:49.550 --> 00:40:53.680
of the principles of
freedom and justice

00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:56.830
are far more precious
to us than anything

00:40:56.830 --> 00:41:00.745
which scientific
discoveries could bestow.

00:41:03.310 --> 00:41:09.160
Those whose minds are
attracted or compelled

00:41:09.160 --> 00:41:12.906
to rigid and symmetrical
systems of government

00:41:12.906 --> 00:41:17.140
should remember that
logic, like science,

00:41:17.140 --> 00:41:21.376
must be the servant and
not the master of man.

00:41:21.376 --> 00:41:23.841
[APPLAUSE]

00:41:29.280 --> 00:41:32.760
Human beings and human
societies are not

00:41:32.760 --> 00:41:38.330
structures that are built,
or machines that are forged.

00:41:38.330 --> 00:41:44.190
They are plants that grow
and must be tended as such.

00:41:44.190 --> 00:41:49.400
Life is a test, and this
world a place of trial.

00:41:49.400 --> 00:41:54.090
Always the problems-- or it
may be the same problem--

00:41:54.090 --> 00:41:59.580
will be presented to every
generation in different forms.

00:41:59.580 --> 00:42:01.680
The problems of victory
may even be more

00:42:01.680 --> 00:42:05.610
baffling than those of defeat.

00:42:05.610 --> 00:42:09.540
However much the
conditions change,

00:42:09.540 --> 00:42:16.170
the supreme question is how
we live and grow and bloom

00:42:16.170 --> 00:42:21.450
and die, and how far
each human life conforms

00:42:21.450 --> 00:42:25.680
to standards, which
are not wholly related

00:42:25.680 --> 00:42:29.640
to space or time.

00:42:29.640 --> 00:42:33.420
And here I speak
not only to those

00:42:33.420 --> 00:42:38.550
who enjoy the blessings
and consolation

00:42:38.550 --> 00:42:42.240
of revealed religion,
but also to those

00:42:42.240 --> 00:42:47.910
who face the mysteries
of human destiny alone.

00:42:47.910 --> 00:42:51.630
I say that the flame
of Christian ethics

00:42:51.630 --> 00:42:54.360
is still our highest guide.

00:42:54.360 --> 00:42:58.160
To guard and cherish it
is our first interest,

00:42:58.160 --> 00:43:01.800
both spiritually and materially.

00:43:01.800 --> 00:43:05.820
The fulfillment of spiritual
beauty in our daily life

00:43:05.820 --> 00:43:08.690
is vital to our survival.

00:43:08.690 --> 00:43:12.870
Only by bringing it into
perfect application can

00:43:12.870 --> 00:43:19.670
we hope to solve for ourselves
the problems of this world,

00:43:19.670 --> 00:43:21.641
and not of this world alone.

00:43:26.260 --> 00:43:32.380
Ladies and gentlemen, I cannot
speak to you here tonight

00:43:32.380 --> 00:43:37.800
without expressing
to the United States,

00:43:37.800 --> 00:43:40.590
as I have perhaps
some right to do,

00:43:40.590 --> 00:43:46.410
the thanks of Britain and of
Europe for the splendid part

00:43:46.410 --> 00:43:50.370
America is playing in the world.

00:43:50.370 --> 00:43:57.420
We seek nothing from Russia
but goodwill and fair play.

00:43:57.420 --> 00:44:01.290
If, however, there is
to be a war of nerves,

00:44:01.290 --> 00:44:05.940
let us make sure that our
nerves are strong and are

00:44:05.940 --> 00:44:10.000
fortified by the deepest
convictions of our hearts.

00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:13.430
[APPLAUSE]

00:44:16.870 --> 00:44:22.040
If we persevere steadfastly
together and allow

00:44:22.040 --> 00:44:27.330
no appeasement of tyranny
and wrongdoing in any form,

00:44:27.330 --> 00:44:30.110
it may not be our
nerve or the structure

00:44:30.110 --> 00:44:33.110
of our civilized nation
which will break.

00:44:33.110 --> 00:44:38.309
Something else will break, and
peace may yet be preserved.

00:44:38.309 --> 00:44:40.774
[APPLAUSE]

00:44:43.250 --> 00:44:48.040
Many nations have risen to
the summit of human affairs,

00:44:48.040 --> 00:44:53.820
but here is a great example
where new-won supremacy has not

00:44:53.820 --> 00:44:57.920
been used for
self-aggrandizement, but only

00:44:57.920 --> 00:45:00.464
for further sacrifice.

00:45:00.464 --> 00:45:03.326
[APPLAUSE]

00:45:09.050 --> 00:45:15.770
Three years ago, I made a
speech at Fulton, Missouri,

00:45:15.770 --> 00:45:19.250
under the auspices
of President Truman.

00:45:19.250 --> 00:45:22.640
Many people here, and
in my own country,

00:45:22.640 --> 00:45:27.350
were startled and even
shocked by what I said.

00:45:27.350 --> 00:45:29.750
But events have
vindicated and fulfilled

00:45:29.750 --> 00:45:34.820
in much detail the warnings
which I deemed it my duty

00:45:34.820 --> 00:45:37.710
to give at that time.

00:45:37.710 --> 00:45:42.960
Today, there is a very
different climate of opinion.

00:45:42.960 --> 00:45:51.080
I'm in cordial accord with
much that is being done.

00:45:51.080 --> 00:45:56.240
We have as dominating facts
the famous [INAUDIBLE],,

00:45:56.240 --> 00:46:02.840
the new unity in Western Europe,
and now the Atlantic Pact.

00:46:02.840 --> 00:46:08.250
How has this tremendous change
in our outlook and policy

00:46:08.250 --> 00:46:09.842
been accomplished?

00:46:09.842 --> 00:46:12.510
Let us inquire into that.

00:46:12.510 --> 00:46:16.700
The responsible ministers in
all the countries concerned

00:46:16.700 --> 00:46:18.686
deserve high credit.

00:46:18.686 --> 00:46:21.860
There is credit enough for all.

00:46:21.860 --> 00:46:28.190
In my own country, the
foreign secretary, Mr. Bevin,

00:46:28.190 --> 00:46:32.600
who has come here tonight
to sign the Atlantic Pact,

00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:37.010
has shown himself, like
many American public men,

00:46:37.010 --> 00:46:41.030
above mere partisan
interest in dealing

00:46:41.030 --> 00:46:45.800
with these national
and world issues.

00:46:45.800 --> 00:46:48.205
[APPLAUSE]

00:46:51.580 --> 00:46:53.860
No one could,
however, have brought

00:46:53.860 --> 00:46:58.210
about these immense changes
in the feeling of the United

00:46:58.210 --> 00:47:02.150
States, of Great
Britain, and of Europe,

00:47:02.150 --> 00:47:07.960
but for the astounding policy of
the Russian Soviet government.

00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:13.250
We may well ask, why have
they deliberately acted

00:47:13.250 --> 00:47:17.880
for three long years so as
to unite the free world again

00:47:17.880 --> 00:47:19.750
them?

00:47:19.750 --> 00:47:22.000
It is certainly not
because there are not

00:47:22.000 --> 00:47:24.640
some very able men among them.

00:47:24.640 --> 00:47:27.160
Why, then, have they done it?

00:47:27.160 --> 00:47:34.510
I will offer you my own answer
to this strange conundrum.

00:47:34.510 --> 00:47:39.760
It is because they fear the
friendship of the West more

00:47:39.760 --> 00:47:41.856
than its hostility.

00:47:41.856 --> 00:47:47.860
They cannot-- they cannot afford
to allow free and friendly

00:47:47.860 --> 00:47:53.770
intercourse to grow up between
the vast areas they control

00:47:53.770 --> 00:47:57.280
and the civilization
of the West.

00:47:57.280 --> 00:48:01.510
The Russian people must not
see what is going on outside,

00:48:01.510 --> 00:48:03.640
and the world must
not see what goes on

00:48:03.640 --> 00:48:07.780
inside the Soviet domain.

00:48:07.780 --> 00:48:11.380
13 men in the
Kremlin, holding down

00:48:11.380 --> 00:48:14.890
hundreds of millions
of people and aiming

00:48:14.890 --> 00:48:18.480
at the rule of the world,
feel that at all costs

00:48:18.480 --> 00:48:21.820
they must keep up the barriers.

00:48:21.820 --> 00:48:27.790
Self-preservation-- not for
Russia, but for themselves--

00:48:27.790 --> 00:48:31.210
lies at the root and
is the explanation

00:48:31.210 --> 00:48:34.040
of their sinister
and malignant policy.

00:48:37.016 --> 00:48:39.496
[APPLAUSE]

00:48:46.440 --> 00:48:51.930
In consequence of
the Soviet conduct,

00:48:51.930 --> 00:48:55.300
the relations of
communist Russia

00:48:55.300 --> 00:48:57.850
with the other great
powers of the world

00:48:57.850 --> 00:49:00.810
are without
precedent in history.

00:49:00.810 --> 00:49:03.390
Measures and
countermeasures have

00:49:03.390 --> 00:49:08.310
been taken on many occasions,
which in any previous period

00:49:08.310 --> 00:49:13.020
could only have meant or
accompanied armed conflict.

00:49:13.020 --> 00:49:16.170
The situation has
been well described

00:49:16.170 --> 00:49:21.210
by distinguished
Americans as the Cold War.

00:49:21.210 --> 00:49:26.640
And the question is asked,
are we winning the Cold War?

00:49:26.640 --> 00:49:30.820
Well, this cannot be decided
by looking at Europe alone.

00:49:30.820 --> 00:49:33.680
We must also look at Asia.

00:49:33.680 --> 00:49:38.610
The worst disaster
since our victory

00:49:38.610 --> 00:49:44.010
has been the collapse of
China under communist attack

00:49:44.010 --> 00:49:48.870
and in [? creed. ?] China, in
which the United States have

00:49:48.870 --> 00:49:54.360
always taken a high interest,
comprises an immense part

00:49:54.360 --> 00:49:57.060
of the population of the world.

00:49:57.060 --> 00:50:01.680
The absorption of
China and of India

00:50:01.680 --> 00:50:05.250
into the Kremlin-controlled
communist empire

00:50:05.250 --> 00:50:07.320
would certainly
bring measureless

00:50:07.320 --> 00:50:11.880
bloodshed and misery to
800 or 900 million people.

00:50:15.160 --> 00:50:17.890
On the other hand,
the position in Europe

00:50:17.890 --> 00:50:21.760
has so far been
successfully maintained.

00:50:21.760 --> 00:50:24.370
The prodigious effort
of the Berlin airlift

00:50:24.370 --> 00:50:27.610
has carried us
through the winter.

00:50:27.610 --> 00:50:33.016
Time, though dearly bought,
has been gained for peace.

00:50:33.016 --> 00:50:38.450
The efficiency of the American
and British air forces

00:50:38.450 --> 00:50:42.670
has been proved and improved.

00:50:42.670 --> 00:50:47.770
Most of all, the spectacle
of the British and Americans

00:50:47.770 --> 00:50:51.370
trying to feed the 2
million Germans in Berlin,

00:50:51.370 --> 00:50:55.030
in their zone in Berlin,
while the Soviet government

00:50:55.030 --> 00:50:59.290
was trying to starve them
out, has been an object lesson

00:50:59.290 --> 00:51:02.770
to the German people,
far beyond anything

00:51:02.770 --> 00:51:05.770
that words could convey.

00:51:05.770 --> 00:51:10.320
I trust that small and
needless provocations

00:51:10.320 --> 00:51:15.940
of German sentiment may be
avoided by the Western powers.

00:51:15.940 --> 00:51:20.660
The revival and union of Europe
cannot be achieved without

00:51:20.660 --> 00:51:25.970
the earnest and freely given
aid of the German people.

00:51:25.970 --> 00:51:33.770
This has certainly been promoted
by the Berlin airlift, which

00:51:33.770 --> 00:51:37.760
has fully justified itself.

00:51:37.760 --> 00:51:43.570
Nevertheless, ladies and
gentlemen, fear and its shadows

00:51:43.570 --> 00:51:47.730
brood over Western Europe today.

00:51:47.730 --> 00:51:52.990
A month ago, in Brussels,
I spoke to a meeting

00:51:52.990 --> 00:51:56.380
of 30,000 Belgians.

00:51:56.380 --> 00:52:03.250
I could feel at once their
friendship and their anxiety.

00:52:03.250 --> 00:52:08.260
They have no Atlantic
Ocean, no English Channel,

00:52:08.260 --> 00:52:13.810
between them and the Russian
communist armored divisions.

00:52:13.810 --> 00:52:16.480
Yet they bravely
and ardently support

00:52:16.480 --> 00:52:20.198
the cause of united Europe.

00:52:20.198 --> 00:52:22.160
I admired them.

00:52:22.160 --> 00:52:25.140
I was also conscious
of the hope and faith

00:52:25.140 --> 00:52:27.960
which lay, like
the Greek people,

00:52:27.960 --> 00:52:31.810
place in the United States.

00:52:31.810 --> 00:52:36.720
I could see the movement
of this vast crowd

00:52:36.720 --> 00:52:38.940
when I spoke of the hands--

00:52:38.940 --> 00:52:42.060
strong hand-- stretched
out across the ocean

00:52:42.060 --> 00:52:44.930
by the great republic.

00:52:44.930 --> 00:52:49.160
You have great
responsibilities there,

00:52:49.160 --> 00:52:52.060
for much faith is
placed upon you.

00:52:52.060 --> 00:52:57.700
I must not conceal from you
tonight the truth as I see it.

00:52:57.700 --> 00:53:03.480
It is certain that Europe
would have been communized,

00:53:03.480 --> 00:53:08.380
like Czechoslovakia, and
London under bombardment

00:53:08.380 --> 00:53:11.560
some time ago, but
for the deterrent

00:53:11.560 --> 00:53:14.902
of the atomic bomb in the
hands of the United States.

00:53:14.902 --> 00:53:17.705
[APPLAUSE]

00:53:25.570 --> 00:53:29.395
Another question is also asked--

00:53:29.395 --> 00:53:33.184
is time on our side?

00:53:33.184 --> 00:53:34.600
This, ladies and
gentlemen, is not

00:53:34.600 --> 00:53:40.120
a question that can be answered
except within strict limits.

00:53:40.120 --> 00:53:44.260
We have certainly not an
unlimited period of time

00:53:44.260 --> 00:53:47.640
before a settlement
should be achieved.

00:53:47.640 --> 00:53:51.140
The utmost vigilance
should be practiced,

00:53:51.140 --> 00:53:55.520
but I do not think
myself that violent

00:53:55.520 --> 00:54:00.370
or [? precipitate ?]
action should be taken now.

00:54:00.370 --> 00:54:03.220
War is not inevitable.

00:54:03.220 --> 00:54:06.940
The Germans have a wise
saying that trees do not

00:54:06.940 --> 00:54:09.520
grow up to the sky.

00:54:09.520 --> 00:54:13.120
Often something happens
to turn or mitigate

00:54:13.120 --> 00:54:15.760
the course of events.

00:54:15.760 --> 00:54:20.610
400 or 500 years
ago, Europe seemed

00:54:20.610 --> 00:54:24.400
about to be conquered
by the Mongols.

00:54:24.400 --> 00:54:28.180
Two great battles were fought
almost on the same day,

00:54:28.180 --> 00:54:31.750
near Vienna and in Poland.

00:54:31.750 --> 00:54:36.790
In both of these, the chivalry
and armed power of Europe

00:54:36.790 --> 00:54:42.610
was completely shattered
by the Asiatic hordes

00:54:42.610 --> 00:54:45.460
of mounted archers.

00:54:45.460 --> 00:54:48.330
It seemed that
nothing could avert

00:54:48.330 --> 00:54:51.130
the doom of the famous
continent, from which

00:54:51.130 --> 00:54:53.980
modern civilization
and culture had

00:54:53.980 --> 00:54:56.440
spread throughout the world.

00:54:56.440 --> 00:55:00.490
But at a critical moment,
something happened.

00:55:00.490 --> 00:55:02.982
The great Khan died.

00:55:02.982 --> 00:55:06.910
The succession was vacant,
and the Mongol armies

00:55:06.910 --> 00:55:10.985
and their leaders trooped
back on their ponies

00:55:10.985 --> 00:55:14.650
to cross the 7,000 miles
which separated them

00:55:14.650 --> 00:55:19.660
from their capital in order
to choose a successor.

00:55:19.660 --> 00:55:23.815
They never returned-- till now.

00:55:23.815 --> 00:55:26.290
[APPLAUSE]

00:55:32.240 --> 00:55:36.420
We need not abandon
hope or patience.

00:55:36.420 --> 00:55:39.860
Many favorable
processes are on foot.

00:55:39.860 --> 00:55:43.190
Under the impact of communism,
all the free nations

00:55:43.190 --> 00:55:47.480
are being welded together as
they never have been before

00:55:47.480 --> 00:55:51.920
and never could be, but for
the harsh external pressure

00:55:51.920 --> 00:55:54.380
to which they are
being subjected.

00:55:54.380 --> 00:55:58.250
We have no hostility to the
Russian people and no desire

00:55:58.250 --> 00:56:03.300
to deny them their legitimate
rights and security.

00:56:03.300 --> 00:56:06.560
I hoped that Russia,
after the war,

00:56:06.560 --> 00:56:10.460
would have access
to unfrozen waters,

00:56:10.460 --> 00:56:15.610
into every ocean, guaranteed by
the world organization of which

00:56:15.610 --> 00:56:18.230
she be a leading member.

00:56:18.230 --> 00:56:21.780
I hoped that she would have the
freest access, which indeed she

00:56:21.780 --> 00:56:26.370
has at the present time, to
raw materials of every kind,

00:56:26.370 --> 00:56:30.160
and that Russians everywhere
would be received as brothers

00:56:30.160 --> 00:56:32.840
in the human family.

00:56:32.840 --> 00:56:36.902
That still remains
our aim and our ideal.

00:56:36.902 --> 00:56:40.206
[APPLAUSE]

00:56:43.510 --> 00:56:48.510
This is a hard experience
in the life of the world.

00:56:48.510 --> 00:56:52.920
After our great victory,
which we believed

00:56:52.920 --> 00:56:59.240
would decide the struggle for
freedom, for our time at least,

00:56:59.240 --> 00:57:04.790
we thought we had deserved
better of fortune.

00:57:04.790 --> 00:57:09.080
But unities and associations
are being established

00:57:09.080 --> 00:57:14.350
by many nations throughout
the free world with a speed

00:57:14.350 --> 00:57:18.830
and reality which would not
have been achieved perhaps

00:57:18.830 --> 00:57:21.590
for generations.

00:57:21.590 --> 00:57:26.300
Of all these unities, the
one most precious to me

00:57:26.300 --> 00:57:34.550
is, to use an expression I used
first at Harvard six years ago,

00:57:34.550 --> 00:57:39.470
the one most precious to me
is the fraternal association

00:57:39.470 --> 00:57:42.950
between the British Commonwealth
of nations and the United

00:57:42.950 --> 00:57:43.927
States.

00:57:43.927 --> 00:57:46.312
[APPLAUSE]

00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:59.200
Do not, my friends, I beg you,
underrate the enduring strength

00:57:59.200 --> 00:58:01.110
of Britain.

00:58:01.110 --> 00:58:05.020
As I said at Fulton, do not
suppose that half a century

00:58:05.020 --> 00:58:09.300
from now, you will not
see 70 or 80 millions

00:58:09.300 --> 00:58:12.100
of Britons spread
about the world

00:58:12.100 --> 00:58:17.380
and united in defense of our
traditions, our way of life,

00:58:17.380 --> 00:58:22.330
and the world causes
which you and we espouse.

00:58:22.330 --> 00:58:24.472
[APPLAUSE]

00:58:27.220 --> 00:58:31.180
United we stand secure.

00:58:31.180 --> 00:58:34.880
Let us then move
forward together

00:58:34.880 --> 00:58:39.950
in this charge of our
mission and our duty,

00:58:39.950 --> 00:58:42.820
fearing God and nothing else.

00:58:42.820 --> 00:58:44.620
[APPLAUSE]

00:59:46.420 --> 01:00:11.970
[MUSIC - "THE STAR SPANGLED
 BANNER"]

